chorus:
Love that wipes the tears from sorrow’s weeping eyes;
Love that lights the gloom and points us to the skies;
All in earth or heav’n that fully satisfies,
Nothing but the love of Jesus

verses:
Nothing held back! on Thee, Jesus, I call;
Thou blessed Savior, so worthy of all;
Loving and dying on Calvary’s tree,
Giving Thy precious last blood drop for me.

O my Redeemer, while Thy throne addressing,
Clear are the visions of glory I see;
Great is my rapture, love like Thine possessing,
Life is an Eden bright wher’er I be;
O my Redeemer, rich in every blessing,
Now and forever do Thou dwell in me.

I cannot falter if Thy hand uphold me,
I cannot wander if close to Thy side;
I cannot weary when Thy word has told me
Thou art my Refuge and my faithful Guide;
O my Redeemer, Thou hast still controlled mw;
Safe in Thy promise will my soul abide.

O my Redeemer, lead the way before me,
Grant that Thy Spirit my light shall be;
Gladly I follow, humbly I adore Thee,
Under Thy loving care I walk with Thee;
O my Redeemer, hear me, I implore Thee,
